1
00:00:00,174 --> 00:00:03,584
Pakistan's farms depend on rivers
that flow through India first.

2
00:00:03,774 --> 00:00:05,390
What if India closed the tap?

3
00:00:05,390 --> 00:00:10,850
The 1960 Indus Waters Treaty gave India
three eastern rivers and Pakistan three

4
00:00:10,850 --> 00:00:12,000
western ones.

5
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:16,850
In 2025, India placed the treaty in
abeyance after the Pahalgam attack.

6
00:00:16,911 --> 00:00:20,741
Pakistan relies on the Indus system
for most of its irrigated farmland,

7
00:00:21,251 --> 00:00:24,261
so any disruption would hit crops,
power and cities.

8
00:00:24,491 --> 00:00:28,121
Reality check: India has limited
storage on the western rivers.

9
00:00:28,297 --> 00:00:31,867
It can delay or regulate flows,
but it can't stop them quickly.

10
00:00:32,042 --> 00:00:33,852
Building that storage takes years,

11
00:00:34,162 --> 00:00:36,852
and the treaty fight now
sits in international law.

12
00:00:36,922 --> 00:00:39,292
Is water a weapon or a shared lifeline?

13
00:00:39,323 --> 00:00:39,953
Comment.

